From ff24d123a7de8d1a015cf95ed30d466d5c4d3411 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Tourniquet
 <254161373+lerapeurdu62280-debug@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:37:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 54/55] Textures the card had no memory for are made again
 later (avatarmanz/VIctory-7900XTX#256)

A host texture refused with E_OUTOFMEMORY was refused for good: the
resource kept no host copy for the rest of the run, its bindless slot was
marked done, and the descriptor cache kept the null view it got.

- The refusal now waits RETRY_MS (500 ms, as uploads do) when the card
  was out of memory, and stays for good for any other error.
- A texture slot whose texture waits so is held in the queue, not done.
- Its descriptor slot is not noted as made, so the next ask makes it.
- A host texture that could not be made resident counts as out of memory
  too (the upload backoff saw only creation failures).

Test: a_texture_refused_for_want_of_memory_is_made_later injects one
E_OUTOFMEMORY (made again after the wait) and one E_INVALIDARG (stays
refused) into the real creation path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit d8d5d20cb013f29381d9f42dd837d866965841da)
(cherry picked from commit 4e95a7837b3dae1633f6d01f3b69dd4dd0f77437)
